# GTM Sprint Context (60-Day Founding Client Acquisition)

## Sprint Overview

**Duration:** 60 days from start date
**Objective:** Secure first 1-3 paid workshops or equivalent engagements (Founding Clients)

**Key Principles:**
- Founder-led sales (sales rep is the founder)
- Targeted experimentation
- Selective use of consultant time on high-leverage activities
- Extensive use of AI tools for production work (email drafting, summarization, content first drafts)

## Sprint Phases

### Phase 1: Segment Selection & ICP Focus
- Review existing relationships, pipeline, market hypotheses
- Identify and prioritize single primary segment
- Articulate ICP, buyer roles/personas, qualification criteria
- Client provides contact lists, CRM access, background materials

### Phase 2: Founding Client Offer Design
- Define structure, scope, outcomes of "Founding Client" Applied AI workshop
- Clarify inclusions/exclusions, delivery format, expected outcomes
- Recommend pricing, incentives (early-adopter discount), simple terms
- Review and improve offer language

### Phase 3: GTM Messaging & Outreach Design
- Refine core sales narratives for target segment
- Create "why now / why this" story for Founding Client Offer
- Develop key objection-handling points and credibility markers
- Design 1 primary outbound email sequence (3-5 touches)
- Create 1-2 LinkedIn message flows
- Build simple call outline or 2-3-slide "conversation anchor"

### Phase 4: High-Impact Deal Support
- Pre-call strategy for selected high-value meetings
- Join limited number of live prospect calls (co-lead or observer)
- Support proposal and close activities on serious opportunities
- Post-call debriefs (live or async) focused on lessons learned and next steps

## Time Allocation

**Consultant services are time-boxed** to maximum hours over 60-day sprint.

**Hours cover:**
- Segment and offer design working sessions
- Messaging and asset review/creation
- Pre-call/post-call strategy
- Limited number of live prospect calls

**AI-Accelerated Work:**
- Client (and/or VA/contractors) generate initial drafts
- AI tools handle production work (drafting, summarization)
- Consultant provides judgment, structure, and refinement

## Client Responsibilities

**Client owns and executes:**
- Detailed list building, enrichment, data entry
- Call scheduling, calendar management, confirmations
- Capturing call notes and action items (using templates/AI tools)
- Building proposal documents and follow-up communications (from templates)
- Sending emails, LinkedIn messages, follow-ups
- List management, sequencing tools, CRM updates

**Client provides:**
- Existing contact lists, CRM access, background materials
- Existing materials (framework descriptions, prior decks) to inform offer
- Approval of final pricing and commercial terms

## Consultant Responsibilities

**Consultant provides:**
- Strategic guidance and structure
- High-leverage deal support
- Review and refinement of AI-generated content
- Real-time feedback on live calls
- Lessons learned and workflow adjustments

**Consultant does NOT:**
- Manual production of all assets (AI handles this)
- Broad pipeline activity (focus on high-value deals)
- Detailed list building or data entry

## Success Metrics

**Sprint succeeds if:**
- First 1-3 paid workshops/engagements secured
- Clear segment and ICP defined
- Founding Client Offer designed and tested
- Outreach sequences created and executed
- High-value deals supported through to close

---

**Use this context when guiding workflows. Emphasize founder-led sales, AI-accelerated work, and high-leverage activities.**
